# The two secrets answering from Discord needs, in a file of their own rather than beside
# the webhook: `op run` fails outright on a reference it cannot resolve, so a bot token
# named here before the field exists would stop every alert rather than leaving one feature
# off. hachiko passes this file only when ~/.config/hachiko/discord has a channel and a
# user in it, which is the same moment these fields have to exist.

# The bot, which is what makes answering from Discord possible: a webhook can post and
# nothing else. With it, every message goes through the bot and each incident gets a thread.
# `hachiko listen` resolves it once per start rather than once per poll, so a five-second
# loop costs the service account nothing.
HACHIKO_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=op://dev/hachiko-discord/bot token

# The second factor an action on the never list needs, checked on the Mac so that a Discord
# account somebody has taken over cannot reach one. The field's own value rather than
# `?attribute=otp`, which is the current code: hachiko verifies codes itself and is given
# the secret, never the on-call agent. An otpauth:// URI and a bare base32 secret are both
# read, since which of them `op` answers with for a one-time-password field is 1Password's
# business rather than this one's.
HACHIKO_APPROVAL_TOTP=op://dev/hachiko-discord/approval
